<p>The United States has issued a 30-day waiver that eases some sanctions on Russian oil, with exemptions running until April 11, as President Trump&#x27;s administration tries to calm energy markets rattled by the war involving Iran and fears of Middle East supply disruptions. PBS reported that crude prices stayed high even after the move, underscoring how closely the market is watching the wider regional conflict and the risk of tighter global supply. Ukraine and several European allies criticized the decision, saying that allowing more Russian oil sales could strengthen the Kremlin&#x27;s finances while Russia continues its full-scale invasion of Ukraine. President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said the waiver &quot;certainly does not help to bring peace closer,&quot; and Kyiv warned the measure could send billions more to Moscow at a time when sanctions have aimed to limit Russia&#x27;s war funding.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/0Hs2m5-tRwZR5Penc7DfHDx0ktDiQ_6mS_tUFChY5YIC3qrk94mqTC-Mp5iYp7JKYKknU46F7525ZJ3crWsgojia_-NouCr4tlRz0Qd7jGFgmltf7vrpBCRW4FDu5oROhoxODtXpP0s9PYMktjcZ28FSCNHgCAaOkF3y8sl0WJlJpIAgh4PjswHaZkk2YsizP5VGcqNnupjLDa3W-xkFh_8D78WPc_evLFo' alt='Image tied to reporting on Russian oil trade and energy market disruption during the Iran war.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>At-sea cargoes: The Treasury authorization applies specifically to Russian oil already at sea, not a full rollback of US sanctions policy.</li><li>Kyiv estimate: Ukrainian officials warned that the temporary easing could add about $10 billion to Russia&#x27;s war chest.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ukraine government: Kyiv says the waiver will make it harder to pressure Moscow financially and that extra oil revenue would directly support Russia&#x27;s war effort against Ukraine. (<a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/ukraine-russia-iran-us-oil-sanctions-energy-crisis/33704872.html'>RFE/RL</a>)</li><li>US administration: Washington framed the temporary authorization as a market-stabilizing step meant to ease supply anxiety and reduce pressure on global energy prices during the Iran-related disruption. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-eases-some-sanctions-on-russian-oil-but-crude-prices-remain-high'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>European allies: European capitals say the waiver leaves them squeezed between war-driven energy costs at home and the need to keep sanctions pressure on Moscow rather than loosen it. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/13/ukraine-eu-allies-slam-us-decision-to-roll-back-russia-oil-sanctions'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Iran: Tehran cast the waiver as evidence that turmoil in the Middle East can push Washington to soften its own Russia pressure campaign, and it pointed to India as a public example. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-is-begging-world-india-to-buy-russian-oil-irans-foreign-minister-araghchi/article70742323.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/zelenskyy-us-30-day-waiver-russian-oil-sanctions-131038045'>Zelenskyy says US 30-day waiver on Russian oil sanctions is &#x27;not the right decision&#x27;</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c1d6l67122wo'>Ukraine and allies fear easing Russian sanctions will prolong war</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-eases-some-sanctions-on-russian-oil-but-crude-prices-remain-high'>U.S. eases some sanctions on Russian oil, but crude prices remain high</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/13/ukraine-eu-allies-slam-us-decision-to-roll-back-russia-oil-sanctions'>Ukraine, EU allies slam US decision to roll back Russia oil sanctions</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://meduza.io/en/news/2026/03/13/u-s-temporarily-lifts-sanctions-on-russian-oil-as-middle-east-war-drives-up-energy-prices'>U.S. temporarily lifts sanctions on Russian oil as Middle East war drives up 